## Quotes Service and Tests for it


The Quotes service is the layer responsible for getting the data by querying a data source. It also abstracts out the data source from the caller. For this guide, to keep the scope small, a static array with 17 quotes is used as the data. The Quotes service could have communicated with a relational database or a NoSQL database using an Object Relational Mapper (ORM), but that is out of the scope of a tutorial focused on testing. Below is the code for the Quotes service:


